data.content:
In **EF Core 11** (.NET 11), the **sync-over-async opt-in for the Cosmos DB provider is removed entirely**. The escape hatch you used in .NET 10 (`CosmosOptionsExtension` / `EnableSynchronousOperations`) no longer exists.

**Every synchronous LINQ operator** in your repository will throw an `InvalidOperationException` at runtime:

| Breaks | Replacement |
|---|---|
| `.ToList()` | `await .ToListAsync()` |
| `.First(...)` | `await .FirstAsync(...)` |
| `.Count()` | `await .CountAsync()` |
| `.SaveChanges()` | `await .SaveChangesAsync()` |

**Migrated version:**

```csharp
public class ProductRepository
{
    private readonly CosmosDbContext _context;

    public async Task<List<Product>> GetAllAsync()
    {
        return await _context.Products.ToListAsync();
    }

    public async Task<Product> GetByIdAsync(int id)
    {
        return await _context.Products.FirstAsync(p => p.Id == id);
    }

    public async Task<int> GetCountAsync()
    {
        return await _context.Products.CountAsync();
    }

    public async Task SaveAsync(Product product)
    {
        _context.Products.Add(product);
        await _context.SaveChangesAsync();
    }
}
```

**Key steps:**
1. Make all methods `async Task<T>` (or `async Task` for void)
2. Replace every sync LINQ terminal with its `*Async` counterpart
3. `await` each call
4. Propagate `async`/`await` up through all callers
5. Remove the old `EnableSynchronousOperations` configuration — it will cause a build error since the API no longer exists

The Cosmos SDK has always been async-only; EF Core 11 simply stops hiding that behind a blocking wrapper.
